        "code": {
          "text": "Low back pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Central/paraspinal lumbar ache described as deep stiffness, present for approximately 3 months and worsening over the last month or so; more noticeable for 4–6 weeks. Baseline pain 3/10, flaring to 6/10. Worse with standing and walking; better with sitting and stretching. Morning stiffness lasts approximately 10 minutes then eases. No clear injury."
      }
    },
